{% comment %}
  Stand-in picture for a mega menu tile whose collection has no image of its own.

  A menu tile normally shows `collection.featured_image` — the collection's Image in Shopify
  admin, or failing that its first product's photo. A collection that is empty and has no
  image set leaves the tile showing only its initial, which is what these pictures cover.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  PLACEHOLDERS - these are MiaDonna product photos, kept only until the store's
  own collections have images. Set an Image on the collection in Shopify admin
  (or give it products) and that wins automatically, so a handle can stay on
  these lists after it has a real picture. Clear them to turn the pictures off.
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Three lists rather than one, because each names its file a different way:
  - ENGAGEMENT STYLES ship as assets/style-<handle>.png. They are tall (684x1014), framed
    for the homepage carousel, and the menu fits them whole rather than cropping.
  - WEDDING AND JEWELLERY ship as assets/menu-tile-<handle>.png: squares that fill the tile.
  - LOOSE DIAMONDS reuse the shape photographs the homepage already carries, so
    "oval-diamonds" is served by assets/diamond-shape-oval.png and nothing is duplicated.
    The shop-wide shape collections ("shape-oval", every piece set with an oval stone) borrow
    the same photographs - it is the same cut either way.

  Diamond shapes (round-engagement-rings and so on) and metals are deliberately absent: they
  draw the line art and the colour discs in 'menu-tile-fallback', which is what MiaDonna's own
  menu shows for them too. The four Learn links are absent as well — they point at pages, and
  a guide's artwork is lettering that nothing legible survives at tile size.

  Accepts:
  - handle: {String} the collection handle, e.g. "wedding-bands"

  Outputs the asset file name, or nothing when we ship no picture for that handle.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign style_handles = 'solitaire,side-stone,halo,hidden-halo,three-stone,bridal-sets,vintage,nature-inspired,toi-et-moi,promise' | split: ','
  assign tile_handles = 'wedding-bands,anniversary-rings,eternity-rings,plain-metal-wedding-bands,curved-wedding-bands,stackable-rings,mens-rings,new-in,ready-to-ship,best-sellers,studs,hoops-huggies,dangles-drops,climbers-jackets-cuffs,signature-earrings,tennis-necklaces,pendants,fashion-necklaces,signature-necklaces,tennis-bracelets,bangles-cuffs,fashion-bracelets,signature-bracelets' | split: ','
  assign diamond_shapes = 'round,oval,emerald,cushion,marquise,radiant,pear,princess,asscher,heart' | split: ','

  assign placeholder = ''

  for style_handle in style_handles
    if style_handle == handle
      assign placeholder = 'style-' | append: style_handle | append: '.png'
      break
    endif
  endfor

  if placeholder == ''
    for tile_handle in tile_handles
      if tile_handle == handle
        assign placeholder = 'menu-tile-' | append: tile_handle | append: '.png'
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  if placeholder == ''
    for diamond_shape in diamond_shapes
      assign diamond_handle = diamond_shape | append: '-diamonds'
      assign shape_handle = 'shape-' | append: diamond_shape
      if diamond_handle == handle or shape_handle == handle or diamond_shape == handle
        assign placeholder = 'diamond-shape-' | append: diamond_shape | append: '.png'
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  comment
    Near misses, after every exact match has had its turn: "hidden-halo" must not be
    caught by "halo", and "oval-diamond-rings" should still find the oval photograph.
  endcomment
  if placeholder == ''
    for style_handle in style_handles
      if handle contains style_handle
        assign placeholder = 'style-' | append: style_handle | append: '.png'
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  if placeholder == '' and handle contains 'diamond'
    for diamond_shape in diamond_shapes
      if handle contains diamond_shape
        assign placeholder = 'diamond-shape-' | append: diamond_shape | append: '.png'
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  comment
    Tennis spans two tiles, and Liquid has no parentheses to group the test with,
    so the choice is made here and the chain below only reads the answer.
  endcomment
  assign tennis_necklace = false
  assign tennis_bracelet = false
  if handle contains 'tennis-necklace'
    assign tennis_necklace = true
  elsif handle contains 'tennis-bracelet'
    assign tennis_bracelet = true
  elsif handle contains 'tennis'
    if handle contains 'neck'
      assign tennis_necklace = true
    elsif handle contains 'brace'
      assign tennis_bracelet = true
    endif
  endif

  if placeholder == ''
    if handle contains 'dangle'
      assign placeholder = 'menu-tile-dangles-drops.png'
    elsif handle contains 'ear-cuff' or handle contains 'climber'
      assign placeholder = 'menu-tile-climbers-jackets-cuffs.png'
    elsif handle contains 'hoop' or handle contains 'huggie'
      assign placeholder = 'menu-tile-hoops-huggies.png'
    elsif handle contains 'stud'
      assign placeholder = 'menu-tile-studs.png'
    elsif tennis_necklace
      assign placeholder = 'menu-tile-tennis-necklaces.png'
    elsif tennis_bracelet
      assign placeholder = 'menu-tile-tennis-bracelets.png'
    elsif handle contains 'pendant'
      assign placeholder = 'menu-tile-pendants.png'
    elsif handle contains 'curved'
      assign placeholder = 'menu-tile-curved-wedding-bands.png'
    elsif handle contains 'stackable'
      assign placeholder = 'menu-tile-stackable-rings.png'
    elsif handle contains 'eternity'
      assign placeholder = 'menu-tile-eternity-rings.png'
    elsif handle contains 'anniversary'
      assign placeholder = 'menu-tile-anniversary-rings.png'
    elsif handle contains 'plain-metal'
      assign placeholder = 'menu-tile-plain-metal-wedding-bands.png'
    elsif handle contains 'mens' or handle contains 'men'
      assign placeholder = 'menu-tile-mens-rings.png'
    endif
  endif

  echo placeholder
-%}
